# dsh plugins declared by the deployment layer. The entrypoint runs
# `dsbot-plugins sync` on every start: anything already installed is skipped
# without touching the network, only missing plugins are installed. Copy this to
# plugins.txt next to it to take effect.
#
# One spec per line; `#` starts a comment.
#
#   some-plugin@1.2.3          npm package, pinned: a different installed
#                              version is replaced
#   some-plugin                npm package, unpinned: install once, then leave it
#   @scope/pkg@^2.0.0          scoped names work the same way
#   my-plugin                  a directory in overlay/plugins/my-plugin
#   /mnt/elsewhere/other       explicit path (relative paths resolve against
#                              this file)
#
# Local directories are staged into the volume at /data/.overlay-plugins/<name>
# (node_modules and .git are skipped) and then linked, because pnpm cannot write
# into a read-only mount.
#
# Inside the container:
#   dsbot-plugins list
#   dsbot-plugins sync --dry-run
#   dsbot-plugins sync --force      # restage local plugins
#
# A plugin declared here and removed at runtime is installed again on the next
# start. If that is not what you want, bake it into the image instead.

# some-plugin@1.2.3
# my-local-plugin
